## State you track

Three places, kept apart throughout:

- **repo** — the git work tree `ccc` launched you in (`--cwd`). **HEAD
  check**, round measurement, increments, squashes and pushes happen here,
  and only here.
- **working dir** — the directory of `user-request.md`; every artifact lives
  in it. It may be inside the repo or not.
- **artifact repo** — the git repository containing the working dir; the
  repo itself when the working dir is inside it. Every git command you run
  against it carries `-C <working dir>`: your shell's cwd is the repo, and a
  bare `git commit` there lands in the wrong repository.

| State | Initial | Changes when |
|---|---|---|
| **original base** | HEAD at setup | never; the ship squash resets to it |
| **branch** | `git symbolic-ref --short HEAD` at setup | never; **HEAD check** re-attaches to it |
| **freeze** | commit locking the spec set | re-recorded when an approved delta is committed |
| **design `R`** | 1 | every design or delta re-review, including post-freeze; never resets |
| **implementation `R`** | 1 | each intermediate squash |
| **round base** | original base | each intermediate squash → the squash commit; a ship-gate change request → current HEAD |
| **increment `I`** | 0 | each committed increment; reset at round start |
{% if split %}
| **`P`, `S`, retries** | 1, 1, 0 | per unit: `P` on each replan, `S` on each respawn or replan, retries on either; all reset when a unit starts |
{% endif %}
| **round state** | open | *open* from the first increment launch → *in review* when you launch its review → *finished* when the review passes |
| **HEAD** | original base | every squash; otherwise only by **HEAD check** after a launch returns — never from a reply |
| **reviewed HEAD** | — | the HEAD the last reviewer wave saw, per round |
| **`N`, `K`** | 1 | next delta / triage{% if scanner %} / scan{% endif %}{% if sweep %} / sweep-exception{% endif %}{% if forester %} / forester-gate{% endif %} ordinal; task-wide |
{% if fg_design or fg_triage %}
| **`G`** | 1 | forester gate round within one design or triage gate; += 1 each time its notes go down and a revision comes back; reset to 1 whenever a gate clears — design approved, or the designer's re-triage returns `resume` or `delta` |
{% endif %}
| **carried paths** | none | triage dispositions{% if scanner %} and scan reports{% endif %}{% if forester %}, forester rulings{% if decide %} and userproxy notes{% endif %}{% endif %} to list at the next gate |

The two `R` counters are independent.

## Standard payload

Every prompt carries what exists of: working dir, request path, design path
and **every** delta path, log path, round base, current HEAD, the relevant
`R`, the mode (for roles with modes), the target output path, and one
instruction: "Write to file. Reply with the status line only."

Each launch below lists only additions (+) and deliberate omissions (−).

## Replies

Every subagent ends its reply with one line:

```
[agent] status=<OK|RETRY|ESCALATE> result=<token|-> out=<abs-path|-> commit=<hash|->
```

`OK` completed; `result` says which normal outcome. `RETRY` cannot proceed, and
the remedy is a relaunch you perform by table lookup. `ESCALATE` goes up: `out`
is the document saying why, and the route is **Triage** after the freeze, the
design gate before it. You never read `out`; you pass it on.

**A missing or unparsable line is `ESCALATE`** with `out` = the target path
you gave the agent — except from a reviewer, where it is `findings`. A
cut-off launch has no line at all: recover it (**Cut-off launch**); only an
unrecovered launch is a **Launch failure**.

**`commit=` is advisory.** Whether a launch committed is decided by **HEAD
check**, never by the reply. Agents under-report: one that escalates or
retries mid-work often omits the commit it already made.

| Role | `OK` result | `RETRY` result | Extra key |
|---|---|---|---|
