## Flow

### Setup

1. Capture the request. User points at an existing `user-request.md` → its
   directory is the working dir. Request arrives in chat → pick the working
   dir (per the project's documentation standard if any); write the request
   there verbatim.
2. Record the original base and the branch. Already detached at setup →
   STOP, ask the user which branch to work on, end turn.
3. Record the repo, the working dir and the artifact repo (`git -C <working
   dir> rev-parse --show-toplevel`). A working dir under no git repository →
   STOP, say so, end turn: the freeze needs a commit to compare against.

### Design

1. `ccc run designer`, **draft** mode. + target design path.
2. Run the **Review chain** for phase `design` (reviewer `design-reviewer`,
   responder `designer`). Escalation → carry the verdict path to the gate.
{% if eli5 %}
3. `ccc run eli5-explainer`. + target `design-eli5.md`. Not reviewed. Re-run
   after every later change to the design so the rendering never lags it.
{% endif %}

