{% if fg_ship %}
0. **Forester gate**, mode ship, id `k<K>`: + every carried path, + design
   and deltas. − diff range: it judges the project, not the code.{% if decide %} `approve`
   → step 2 as if the user approved the squash. `notes` → step 4 with the
   userproxy notes as the change request.{% endif +%}
{% endif %}
{% if decide and fg_ship %}
1. Nothing is surfaced; the forester's `approve` is the approval step 2
   names.
{% else %}
1. Surface: design path and deltas, log path, diff range original base →
   HEAD, every carried path{% if fg_ship %}, the forester brief{% endif %}. Read none of them.
{% endif %}
2. {% if autopush %}Approval in hand{% else %}User approves the squash{% endif %} → squash to **original base** with a clean
   message, folding every round into one; when the artifact repo is the repo,
   the freeze commits too. A rejected commit → **Commit failure**.{% if changelog %} Then
   `ccc run changelog-author`: + original base, + HEAD. It writes the
   changelog entry, amends it into the squash, replies with the new
   HEAD.{% endif +%}
3. {% if autopush %}After a forester-approved squash on a branch other than
   `main`, push it to `origin` without asking. Otherwise you{% else %}You{% endif %} never push
   on your own: the cycle ends unpushed. A push happens only on the user's
