## Procedures

### Review chain

Parameters: phase, reviewer(s). Pre-freeze escalations carry to the user
gate; post-freeze escalations go to **Triage**.

1. Reviewer(s) → `notes-<phase>-<reviewer>-r<R>.md`. All `no-findings` → the
   chain passes; keep the notes files, launch no responder or judge.
{% if commentator %}
   Otherwise **Commentary** for step `<phase>-r<R>-a1`.
{% endif %}
2. **Respond step** `<phase>-r<R>-a1` (design phase: `designer`, **respond**
   mode; code phase: see below). + notes path(s){% if commentator %}, + commentary path{% endif %}.
3. `ccc run judge`, round 1 → `judge-verdict-<phase>-r<R>-a1.md`. + every
   notes path, + dispositions path{% if commentator %}, + every commentary path{% endif %}, + (design phase) the document / (code
   phase) round base, HEAD, reviewed HEAD, + any triage dispositions path.
4. `rework` → one rework: **Respond step** `<phase>-r<R>-a2` (+ verdict path);
   judge round 2 told "round 2 — approved or escalate only" →
   `judge-verdict-<phase>-r<R>-a2.md`.
5. `approved` → passes. `ESCALATE` → escalation route.

### Respond step — code phases

Parameter: the step id `<step>`. Target `dispositions-<step>.md`; + notes
paths, round, any triage dispositions path and delta path{% if commentator %}, the step's
commentary path where one exists (rework steps have none){% endif %}; a rework step adds
the verdict path.

{% if split %}
Two launches, the increment loop in miniature; the dispositions document plays
the plan. Both get **the round's plans**: every `plan-r<R>-i<I>-p<P>.md` of
every increment in the round, all generations. − request path.

1. `ccc run planner`, **respond** mode. + exception
   `exception-<step>-planner-p<P>.md`; + on a replan, the {{ wshort }}'s
   exception document. `dispositioned`, `delta-complete` or `delta-remaining`
   → step 2, remembering the delta token for **Where a delta lands**.
   `ESCALATE` → **Triage**.
2. `ccc run {{ worker }}`. + dispositions path, unit id `<step>`, starting
   HEAD, exception `exception-<step>-s<S>.md`, handoff `handoff-<step>-s<S>.md`;
   + on a respawn, the previous handoff document. **HEAD check** on every
   status. `done` → the chain continues. `replan` → `S` += 1; step 1; the planner revises the
   dispositions document in place. `respawn` → step 2. `ESCALATE` →
   **Triage**. Retries are capped as in **Implementation**.
{% else %}
`ccc run implementer`, **respond** mode. + exception `exception-<step>.md`.
**HEAD check** on every status. `ESCALATE` → **Triage**.
{% endif %}

### Launch failure

An unrecovered launch (**Cut-off launch**) → **HEAD check** (a cut-off
implementer may have committed), then STOP: surface what that section
lists, the stderr cut to at most two lines;
`status=ESCALATE result=- out=-`. Not triaged: nobody wrote anything to triage. When the user resumes
you: a session id is known → `ccc resume <session id> "Continue."`; none →
repeat the launch verbatim, same paths. Route the reply as the original
launch's.

### HEAD check

A recovery in progress is the same launch: between a cut-off and its resume
you do nothing in the repo. After **every** launch is over — its reply in
hand, or **Launch failure** reached — any role, any status, `commit=` filled
or not — in the repo:

1. **Attachment.** `git symbolic-ref -q HEAD`. Detached (agents do this by
   accident) → re-attach before anything else: if the branch tip is an
   ancestor of HEAD, `git branch -f <branch> HEAD && git checkout <branch>`
   (a no-op move when they are equal). Branch tip not an ancestor, or HEAD
   on another branch → **Repo anomaly**. Commits made while detached are
   then ordinary commits, handled by step 2.
2. **Movement.** `git rev-parse HEAD` against recorded HEAD. The ref is the
   truth; the reply is not.

- Unchanged → nothing was committed. Ignore any `commit=` value.
- Moved, and recorded HEAD is an ancestor (`git merge-base --is-ancestor
  <recorded> HEAD`) → the launch committed, whatever its status line says.
  From a role whose table row has no `+ commit` → **Repo anomaly** first.
  Then record the new HEAD; **Frozen-set check**{% if sweep %}; **Comment sweep** unless the
  launch was the sweep itself{% endif %}. Then route on the status line as written: a
  stop still stops, with the commits in place. Every commit between old and
  new HEAD is in the round (round base → HEAD) and reaches its review and
  judge that way, reported or not.
- Moved elsewhere (reset, rebase, branch switch) → **Repo anomaly**.

### Repo anomaly

The repository is not where your record says. You never guess which is
right. `K` += 1. Two repairs exist, and you state which are on the table:

- `adopt` — the repository as found becomes the record: current HEAD is
  recorded HEAD; if detached, `git checkout -B <branch>` here; if on another
  branch, that branch is now **branch**. Offered only while round base stays
  an ancestor of HEAD; otherwise no round can be measured from it.
- `restore` — `git checkout -B <branch> <recorded HEAD>`. The dropped
  commits stay in the reflog; the ruling names their hashes.

